import mundane theorem    stdlib/geometry/distance-by-coordinates

theorem right-isosceles-triangle
  note        Each side is read off the coordinates. The long side squared is
              50, and so is the sum of the squares of the two short ones.
  let A be a point                                                    (H1)
  let B be a point                                                    (H2)
  let C be a point                                                    (H3)
  assume A = (−2, −1)                                                 (H4)
  assume B = (2, 2)                                                   (H5)
  assume C = (5, −2)                                                  (H6)
  then |AB| = 5. |BC| = 5. |AC|² = |AB|² + |BC|².

1.  |(−2, −1)(2, 2)| = √((−2 − 2)² + (−1 − 2)²)
    mun:distance-by-coordinates

2.  |A(2, 2)| = √((−2 − 2)² + (−1 − 2)²)
    substitute A = (−2, −1) (H4) into line 1

3.  |AB| = √((−2 − 2)² + (−1 − 2)²)
    substitute B = (2, 2) (H5) into line 2

4.  |AB| = 5
    calculation
      |AB| = √((−2 − 2)² + (−1 − 2)²)     3
           = √25                          arithmetic
           = 5                            real arithmetic

5.  |(2, 2)(5, −2)| = √((2 − 5)² + (2 − (−2))²)
    mun:distance-by-coordinates

6.  |B(5, −2)| = √((2 − 5)² + (2 − (−2))²)
    substitute B = (2, 2) (H5) into line 5

7.  |BC| = √((2 − 5)² + (2 − (−2))²)
    substitute C = (5, −2) (H6) into line 6

8.  |BC| = 5
    calculation
      |BC| = √((2 − 5)² + (2 − (−2))²)    7
           = √25                          arithmetic
           = 5                            real arithmetic

9.  |(−2, −1)(5, −2)| = √((−2 − 5)² + (−1 − (−2))²)
    mun:distance-by-coordinates

10. |A(5, −2)| = √((−2 − 5)² + (−1 − (−2))²)
    substitute A = (−2, −1) (H4) into line 9

11. |AC| = √((−2 − 5)² + (−1 − (−2))²)
    substitute C = (5, −2) (H6) into line 10

12. |AC|² = (√((−2 − 5)² + (−1 − (−2))²))²
    substitute |AC| = √((−2 − 5)² + (−1 − (−2))²) (line 11)

13. |AB|² + |BC|² = 5² + |BC|²
    substitute |AB| = 5 (line 4)

14. |AB|² + |BC|² = 5² + 5²
    substitute |BC| = 5 (line 8) into line 13

15. |AC|² = |AB|² + |BC|²
    calculation
      |AC|² = (√((−2 − 5)² + (−1 − (−2))²))²     12
            = 50                                 real arithmetic
            = 5² + 5²                            arithmetic
            = |AB|² + |BC|²                      14

16. |AB| = 5. |BC| = 5. |AC|² = |AB|² + |BC|².
    join 4, 8, 15
